From 1239e8883f8e2f83f62041c4021d53654649ada4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Adler <git@madler.net>
Date: Fri, 3 Apr 2026 19:34:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add compressBound_z, deflateBound_z, xompress_z and uncompress_z functions for large values.

* These take and return size_t integers, instead of unsigned longs,
  for those platforms with 32-bit longs. Overflow is clamped to the
  maximum value for the type.
* Provide size_t arguments for Windows, on which a long is 32 bits.
* Check for invalid NULL pointer inputs to zlib operations.

Upstream: https://github.com/madler/zlib/commit/916dc1ac
Upstream: https://github.com/madler/zlib/commit/4edb00de
Upstream: https://github.com/madler/zlib/commit/5c477553

[backported to 2.3.3: deflateBound() keeps the 2.3.3 fallback wrapper
 length of 6 bytes]
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
